From: scottwis <scottwis@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] direct: use non-contiguous allocation on unified memory systems

Upstream PR: https://github.com/elFarto/nvidia-vaapi-driver/pull/485

Passing NVOS32_ATTR_PHYSICALITY_CONTIGUOUS for NV01_MEMORY_SYSTEM causes
allocations larger than 4 MiB to fail with NV_ERR_NO_MEMORY (51) on 4 KiB-page
kernels with CONFIG_ARCH_FORCE_MAX_ORDER=10 (e.g., NVIDIA N1X / unified-memory
systems), breaking VA-API hardware decode above ~2560x1440.

Use NVOS32_ATTR_PHYSICALITY_NONCONTIGUOUS when allocating system memory on
unified-memory systems.
---
 src/direct/nv-driver.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/direct/nv-driver.c b/src/direct/nv-driver.c
index 658a2d2..faa0019 100644
--- a/src/direct/nv-driver.c
+++ b/src/direct/nv-driver.c
@@ -507,7 +507,7 @@ bool alloc_memory(const NVDriverContext *context, const uint32_t size, int *fd)
                          DRF_DEF(OS32, _ATTR, _PAGE_SIZE, _BIG) |
                          DRF_DEF(OS32, _ATTR, _DEPTH, _UNKNOWN) |
                          DRF_DEF(OS32, _ATTR, _FORMAT, _BLOCK_LINEAR) |
-                         DRF_DEF(OS32, _ATTR, _PHYSICALITY, _CONTIGUOUS);
+                         DRF_DEF(OS32, _ATTR, _PHYSICALITY, _NONCONTIGUOUS);
     } else {
         // Discrete GPU with local video memory
         memoryClass = NV01_MEMORY_LOCAL_USER;
-- 
